sudo vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config
Look for the line:
#PermitRootLogin yes
Change it to:
PermitRootLogin no
•	no → disables direct root login.
•	yes → allows root login (default is usually yes).
⚡ Tip: Remove the # if it’s commented out.
3.	Restart SSH service to apply changes:
sudo systemctl restart sshd
or (on some systems):
sudo service sshd restart
4.	Verify:
•	Try logging in as root:
